{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/885146-most-broken-or-disgusting-disciplines","id":885146,"title":"Most broken or Disgusting Disciplines","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-07T21:37:50-07:00","id":885146,"title":"Most broken or Disgusting Disciplines","content":"As the title says, which are the most broken, most abused, or disciplines that have just left a sour taste in your mouth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11595-chaos965","name":"Chaos965","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11595_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T22:09:22-07:00","id":885156,"title":"","content":"Requiem Disciplines are super tame.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T22:42:50-07:00","id":885183,"title":"","content":"Ah. so no disciplines that leave that bad taste eh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11595-chaos965","name":"Chaos965","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11595_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T22:56:39-07:00","id":885190,"title":"","content":"Not implying anything by it but the number of merits that improve on Protean probably make other disciplines green with envy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T05:36:50-07:00","id":885308,"title":"","content":"I'm not going to call it &quot;broken&quot; or anything, but I think Obfuscate 3 can become a serious problem to a game. It's less overwhelming power, though, and more a ridiculous tool for spying and murder, even on vampires. If you know for sure that someone is a worse fighter than you, you just win if you can catch them with it and nobody without Auspex really has much of a chance to stop you. It requires so many countermeasures to prevent a player with it from just following any vampire home around dawn to discover their haven, and if they can stay awake (either with a roll or Coil of the Ascendant), they can just freely stake whoever they want...it almost feels like scry and fry in D&amp;D.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T07:47:48-07:00","id":885374,"title":"","content":"You don't require Auspex to pierce Obfuscate anymore, anyone with a decent perception rating can do so. The player just needs to get in the habit of actively searching for clues to indicate an obfuscated person may be nearby not just the obfuscated person. Granted the Obfuscate rating of the user penalizes the perception check on the character but merits like Trained Observer (especially the 1st. Edition version) and Enhanced Senses offsets it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T08:13:11-07:00","id":885387,"title":"","content":"Nightmare 1 is a bit gross when you use it on food...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T09:42:56-07:00","id":885432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/885146-most-broken-or-disgusting-disciplines?p=885374#post885374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't require Auspex to pierce Obfuscate anymore, anyone with a decent perception rating can do so. The player just needs to get in the habit of actively searching for clues to indicate an obfuscated person may be nearby not just the obfuscated person. Granted the Obfuscate rating of the user penalizes the perception check on the character but merits like Trained Observer (especially the 1st. Edition version) and Enhanced Senses offsets it.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't pierce the Obfuscate, though, you just know that they're around. And yeah, having every vampire looking for clues constantly <i>just in case</i> is exactly the kind of nonsense preparation I'm talking about, like making sure every wall in higher level dungeons are dimensionally warded or contain teleport traps or something or that all bad guys walk around constantly nondetected and mind blanked, etc. <br /> <br /> There's no resistance, that's the problem. Only unusual, specific countermeasures do anything, and, well, if the invisible guy is a better fighter than you, he can just abduct you into the abyss and own you one vs. one where nobody can help unless they have Auspex (since just knowing they're there doesn't really help). <br /> <br /> It's actually always bothered me that Obfuscate isn't opposed--it works explicitly with mind control after all. You're literally manipulating people's minds into not paying attention to you/not perceiving you. How is that not call for an opposed roll? In my future games, I intend to house rule it to be an opposed Int + Stealth + Obfuscate vs. Resolve + BP roll, I think. I had the same problem in 1e with Obfuscate, because it was totally free. I thought charging blood in 2e would make it better, but then they added the fact that you can abduct people and fight while completely invisible and it went just right back to the same power level--it might even be <i>more</i> powerful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T10:10:54-07:00","id":885460,"title":"","content":"Eh, balance is what you make of it. Especially in Chronicles of Darkness. All Disciplines have the potential to do some impressive things, but I wouldn't call any of them &quot;overpowered&quot; because I don't run the kind of game where there's an expected power curve to be over or under.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T10:12:30-07:00","id":885463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/885146-most-broken-or-disgusting-disciplines?p=885374#post885374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't require Auspex to pierce Obfuscate anymore, anyone with a decent perception rating can do so. The player just needs to get in the habit of actively searching for clues to indicate an obfuscated person may be nearby not just the obfuscated person. Granted the Obfuscate rating of the user penalizes the perception check on the character but merits like Trained Observer (especially the 1st. Edition version) and Enhanced Senses offsets it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you quote that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T12:04:21-07:00","id":885558,"title":"","content":"Sure, right after you show me where the rules expressly stipulates Auspex is a prerequisite to pierce Obfuscate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T12:35:28-07:00","id":885588,"title":"","content":"Its the latter half of cloak of night. On page 138.<br /> &quot;If another vampire manages to perceive him, through Auspex, attack, or any other means, she can sense his predatory aura and 138 lash out. If she wins the predatory aura contest, Cloak of Night shatters, as does any other use of Obfuscate the vampire made. The vampire can be tracked by indirect clues, as mentioned above. Tracking is an extended action, with the observer rolling Wits + Resolve - Obfuscate. A vampire observer can apply the Blood Potency bonus from Kindred senses. Each roll takes one turn, and the observer must roll more successes than the vampire\u2019s Wits + Stealth + Obfuscate. Teamwork may be applied&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T13:05:24-07:00","id":885617,"title":"","content":"We really could use an expansion on the &quot;Or any other means&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T13:31:05-07:00","id":885645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/885146-most-broken-or-disgusting-disciplines?p=885588#post885588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its the latter half of cloak of night. On page 138.<br /> &amp;quot;If another vampire manages to perceive him, through Auspex, attack, or any other means, she can sense his predatory aura and 138 lash out. If she wins the predatory aura contest, Cloak of Night shatters, as does any other use of Obfuscate the vampire made. The vampire can be tracked by indirect clues, as mentioned above. Tracking is an extended action, with the observer rolling Wits + Resolve - Obfuscate. A vampire observer can apply the Blood Potency bonus from Kindred senses. Each roll takes one turn, and the observer must roll more successes than the vampire\u2019s Wits + Stealth + Obfuscate. Teamwork may be applied&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ^ expanded on any other means<br /> Tracking. <br /> A bag of flour and a fan.<br /> Attacking<br /> An insane perception check <br /> Setting off the sprinklers and seeing what the water hits. Lots of scenarios.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T14:17:24-07:00","id":885696,"title":"","content":"Eh, Requiem disciplines are fairly well balanced against each other. Not surprising, since Vamps are <i>pretty</i> straightforward in terms of what their powers do.<br /> <br /> (By the way, this is the first time I've seen the word disgusting used in this way in <a href=\"http://www.rogermwilcox.com/adnd/\" target=\"_blank\">a <i>long</i> time</a>. Let's call it... 9 years at this point?)<br /> <br /> However, on that note... the <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1_J83T-t9g-87pvtUTKCZIJ2QQzCTOzUclkWJjsvb814/edit#heading=h.3yrs39jq6n1s\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Zirnitra</a> can get bloody ridiculous if you pick the right merits (I'm not even talking Psychokinesis (Fire) or Psychokinesis (Light) here - Apportation is <i>ridiculous</i> if you can stick a proper dice pool behind it), and I <i>sincerely</i> hope that Grafting Unholy Flesh is adjusted before the book comes out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T15:43:22-07:00","id":885742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/885146-most-broken-or-disgusting-disciplines?p=885696#post885696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, Requiem disciplines are fairly well balanced against each other. Not surprising, since Vamps are <i>pretty</i> straightforward in terms of what their powers do.<br /> <br /> (By the way, this is the first time I've seen the word disgusting used in this way in <a href=\"http://www.rogermwilcox.com/adnd/\" target=\"_blank\">a <i>long</i> time</a>. Let's call it... 9 years at this point?)<br /> <br /> However, on that note... the <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1_J83T-t9g-87pvtUTKCZIJ2QQzCTOzUclkWJjsvb814/edit#heading=h.3yrs39jq6n1s\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Zirnitra</a> can get bloody ridiculous if you pick the right merits (I'm not even talking Psychokinesis (Fire) or Psychokinesis (Light) here - Apportation is <i>ridiculous</i> if you can stick a proper dice pool behind it), and I <i>sincerely</i> hope that Grafting Unholy Flesh is adjusted before the book comes out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Coils of the Dragon are insane. In other news, water is wet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T15:58:59-07:00","id":885751,"title":"","content":"I mean, all of them are pretty powerful, but its not like any of them break the game. Vampire powers in general are coercive, so that is something to keep in mind as &quot;disgusting&quot; since it removes free will, but the game isn't exactly complex. <br /> <br /> There's a few Devotions and Scales that are blah, but there are times when they might be handy, so its more of niche thing. Theban and Cruac rituals in the core are crap, and I don't like how the rolls work, truthfully, but that's another matter - Secrets of the Covenant and the Elder book seem to come with some very nice miracles/rituals, so that matter is positive.<br /> <br /> My biggest complaint is more that the core book Disciplines and Devotions are very narrow in scope. Physical enhancements and mind control, primarily. How about blood control? Or shadow magic? Plant powers? Luck cursed? Pretty much all the variety in vampire powers are found in Cruac or a bloodline. Everyone else gets a wide breadth of abilities in their core book (Gifts that do everything under the sun, Arcana that do everything, a wealth of Contracts, etc), while vamps end up getting that variety in ritauls and bloodlines. Even Theban miracles are kind of restrictive*, and Coils, for as neat as they are, don't really add anything new, just refine existing stuff. And that's probably why I think vampire abilities are pretty balanced and &quot;tame&quot; as others put it. Its hard to break things when the scope is narrow.<br /> <br /> * Theban seems to be the &quot;religion&quot; magic. Biblical magics, Cult-of-Ra powers, likely some Islamic and Jewish themed magic. Pick a religion, make magic based on that religion's stories. Which, in my opinion, restricts not only the kinds of miracles you can use, but if we get &quot;Egypt&quot; magic, there's a chance that Lancea Sanctum won't use it. Meanwhile, Cruac is open ended, and basically develops any magic that's thematically appropriate for vampires as well as &quot;pagan&quot; monster abilities, and everyone wants to use everything they can get their hands on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T19:42:16-07:00","id":885903,"title":"","content":"I don't have any problem with them, but Lithopedia allows you to give a first level blood bond to everyone in your territory, which can be as small as a room or as larger than an entire city. It's technically a series of rituals of blood sorcery, not a Discipline.<br /> <br /> And that's everyone, not just every vampire. Only creatures immune to Vinculum aren't affected, and if it would bring you to a third stage Vinculum, you can resist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T20:57:13-07:00","id":885940,"title":"","content":"Zinitra is pretty absurd but if there's one thing that deserved the descriptor &quot;disgusting&quot; it's Carthian Law.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/885146-most-broken-or-disgusting-disciplines?p=885308#post885308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not going to call it &quot;broken&quot; or anything, but I think Obfuscate 3 can become a serious problem to a game. It's less overwhelming power, though, and more a ridiculous tool for spying and murder, even on vampires. If you know for sure that someone is a worse fighter than you, you just win if you can catch them with it and nobody without Auspex really has much of a chance to stop you. It requires so many countermeasures to prevent a player with it from just following any vampire home around dawn to discover their haven, and if they can stay awake (either with a roll or Coil of the Ascendant), they can just freely stake whoever they want...it almost feels like scry and fry in D&amp;D.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pfft, you're better off doing it with Auspex, takes less time and there's no chance of them finding out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9368,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","user":"PrinceRaven","date":". 05-09-2016, 12:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}